  return `

CUSTOM SOUNDS (allowed for this build). The server owner's plan includes custom sounds, so rule 2 is extended: you may also create and edit sound spec files at assets/sounds/<set>.json (nowhere else under assets/). Nxeon renders every spec into mono Ogg Vorbis files, writes sounds.json and the subtitles into the server resource pack and sends it to players on join; you never write audio files, sounds.json or a resource pack yourself.
- One file per SOUND SET (one mob, item or spell), at most ${SS.MAX_SOUND_SETS} files and ${SS.MAX_EVENTS_TOTAL} events in total. The file name is the set name: 2-32 chars, lowercase letters, digits and underscores, starting with a letter; "name" inside must be the same.
- Format (Nxeon SoundSpec v1, JSON): {"version": 1, "name": "<set>", "events": [{"event": "hurt", "role": "hurt", "subtitle": "Banshee shrieks", "category"?: "hostile", "variants": [{"weight"?: 1-10, "layers": [1-${SS.MAX_LAYERS} layers], "processing"?: {...}}]}]} with 1-${SS.MAX_EVENTS_PER_SET} events per set.
- event: 1-24 chars (lowercase, digits, underscore), unique in the set. role decides loudness and maximum length: ${roleLimits}. subtitle is REQUIRED (3-60 chars of plain text): what a player who cannot hear the sound reads, e.g. "Banshee wails". category: the Bukkit SoundCategory the plugin passes: ${SS.SOUND_CATEGORIES.join(", ")} (default hostile for mob roles, player for ability/fire/reload, master for ui).
- 1-${SS.MAX_VARIANTS} variants per event; Minecraft picks one at random by weight, so give ambient, hurt and step 2-4 different variants (other seeds, pitch, layers).
- layer: {"source": ${library ? `"synth:<preset>", "lib:<id>" or "silence"` : `"synth:<preset>" or "silence"`}, "start"?: seconds 0-5 (offset in the variant), "gain"?: dB -40..12, "pitch"?: semitones -24..24 (resampling, so higher is also shorter), "length": seconds 0.01-8 (required for synth and silence${library ? "; trims a library sound" : ""}),${library ? ` "trimStart"?: seconds into a library sound,` : ""} "fadeIn"?/"fadeOut"?: ms, "seed"?: integer (synth: another seed = another take), "params"?: {...} (synth)}.
