- Lengths include tails: the estimate of a variant is its longest layer (start + length / 2^(pitch/12)) plus 0.6 s when reverb is set plus 3 x the echo delay; keep that under the role's maximum above (an ambient bed: layers of 3 s, not 4).
- A custom mob built on a vanilla mob: call entity.setSilent(true) when you spawn or tag it and play its own ambient (a repeating task, every few seconds with some randomness), hurt (EntityDamageEvent), death (EntityDeathEvent), attack and step sounds yourself, so the vanilla sounds do not overlap (on 26.x spawning a monster throws in Peaceful difficulty: check world.getDifficulty() != Difficulty.PEACEFUL first). Players without the pack hear nothing for these keys, so gameplay must not depend on hearing them.
- In modbuilder.json "howToUse", say that players accept the server resource pack when they join to hear the custom sounds.${SOUND_EXAMPLE ? `
- Example spec (synth only): ${SOUND_EXAMPLE}` : ""}`;
}
